 "calendarRule": "a date is a session for a market when any of its assets has a bar; thin when fewer than 50% of that market's then-live assets do",
 "completenessRule": "sessionDates over daysElapsed, where the denominator counts weekdays for every market but calendar days for crypto, and stops at the last date in the data rather than at year end",
 "notes": [
  "A market fetched monthly looks fully covered by the per-asset figures above, because they compare each asset with a calendar built from the same data. calendarCompleteness is the check that catches it, and PSX before 2024 is what it catches.",
  "Sessions outside an asset's own stored range are not gaps here; a short history is a survivorship and seeding question, covered by survivorship/report.json.",
  "Nothing is written to any database: this measures whether a repair is possible and prints the command that would do it. tools/recover_asset.py upserts without deleting, never invents a bar, and verifies the rows it did not touch -- but it is still a production write and is left for the owner to run."
